 ## Background
-EWA Splatting originated from the need to render point-sampled surfaces without aliasing or holes. It was formalized by Zwicker et al. (2001) as "Surface Splatting," using Elliptical Weighted Average (EWA) filters to project object-space reconstruction filters to screen space [S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Gaussian Splatting](946-gaussian-splatting.md) by providing the rasterization backend for 3D Gaussian primitives, approximating the volumetric integral via 2D projections [S1].
